Parse faint (SGR 2)

SGR 2 was ignored and SGR 22 cleared bold only, so faint text -- the
grey half of a modern tool's status line, a shell's de-emphasised
suggestion -- reached the screen at full strength with nothing to say it
was meant to be faint.

Add a dim pen attribute: set by SGR 2, cleared by SGR 22 and 0, saved
and restored with the cursor, reported by DECRQSS and get_penattr, and
handed out as VTermScreenCellAttrs.dim. Each new bit is the LAST in its
bitfield, so no struct grows and no existing bit moves -- an exported
terminal (0008) keeps its layout across versions.

